{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086967-c20-problems-with-inanimae","id":1086967,"title":"C20 Problems with Inanimae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-02T20:09:39-07:00","id":1086967,"title":"C20 Problems with Inanimae","content":"Ok, so for the most part I'm very very happy with the C20 document. Outside lack of Merfolk houses, the only real beef I have is with the Inanimae part. Half the phyla are severely dumbed down from their original form, gaining just free merits instead of the interesting powers. Ondines, in particular, miff me. I know, they had the same ability pretty much as Morganed, but......... Just giving them a free merit? It feels a little rushed. Also, having all their slivers be Unleashed-only when originally they had cantrips is really harsh. It means Inanimae magic is incredibly unreliable and dangerous. Also it contradicts itself in saying all Sliver abilities are chimerical unless taking on the wyrd, but doesn't Unleashing immediately force you to take on their weird? I can understand needing page space, but hsien got, what, 8 pages for their wu tan, and inanimae barely get tw page for their slivers? in fact, their section is TINY compared to hsien and nunnehi.<br /> <br /> Don't take this wrong, I do love the book and the updates, but man.... the inanimae section looks like it just got severely rushed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"